          "kind": "explain",
          "title": "One owner at a time",
          "body": [
            {
              "kind": "p",
              "text": "Every value in Rust has exactly one owner. When the owner goes out of scope, the value is dropped."
            },
            {
              "kind": "p",
              "text": "A String keeps its text on the heap. Writing `let b = a;` doesn't copy that text. It hands ownership from `a` to `b`, and `a` can't be used afterwards."
            },
            {
              "kind": "note",
              "text": "Make a prediction before you check each answer. A wrong guess teaches you more than a lucky one."
            }
